VALUES (653, '0', $t$ASK 653: a lexicon line quoted whole no longer voids an [L2] tag whose Strong's number is in the cited verse$t$,
  $t$In run 42528, 15 of the 30 [L2] tags marked NOT COUNTED were misfires, and all 15 were defender (Oracle) tags. In each the tag's Strong's number is in the cited verse. The tag failed because the Oracle quoted the lexicon line whole and the [L2] check took the etymology words in that line as claimed words ("from σύν and ἔρχομαι", "from ἐπί and a derivative of σκιά", "a primary word (compare ἄνθρωπος)", "from a variation of γένος", "probably akin to χράομαι"). markRoots in the Shared Library marked a word as a root only when it directly follows "from", "root", "derived from", "cognate of/with/to" or "related to"; every other word was core and had to be in the cited verse, so the whole tag was voided. Change, one node (Shared Library, the only copy), two LIB lines, both tagged ASK 653: (1) line 146, ROOTPRE: "compare" and "akin to" are root markers, and "variation of", "derivative of", "prolonged form of" and "form of" are allowed after a marker; (2) line 153, rootAt second pass: a word joined by "and" or "or" to a word already marked root is a root too. Expected effect: such a tag is COUNTED when its own core word or number is in the cited verse. Bounds: the and/or join applies only after a root, so two claimed numbers joined by "and" are both still checked; a root is set aside, never counted as found. Not changed: any other node, the child, the database, a model setting, reasoning. (plan rev 0, ask653/w4/plan653.md md5 fefa1ca5)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write it" at 09:27 CST 2026-11-25 on W4's card (Wall 12150; audit 42332 by W4's post), engine 50ade174 to a5c3001d (426 nodes; the child aad0ad9c unchanged), and read back PASS by W1 (Wall 12152 item 1: W1's fetch of live a5c3001d equals its own rebuild, W4's target and W4's fetch-back, 426 nodes, 0 differences, connections equal; against 50ade174 only the Shared Library differs; standing 31 PASS 0 FAIL). Plan rev 0 PASS WITH N1 (Wall 12125); N1 (a test that a tag holding only an absent "compare X" stays NOT COUNTED; name every changed tag of 42373 on both sides) is met in the build (t653 line N1; 42373 has no changed tag). Build b1 graded PASS by W1 (Wall 12133: W1's own rebuild from live equals the target; only LIB lines 146 and 153 change; t653 14 of 14 run by W1). Offline replay of the [L2] check (W4's build notes; Wall 12133): in 42528, 15 tags change, all defender, all NOT COUNTED to COUNTED (tags 88, 90, 91, 99, 101, 107, 108, 112, 113, 151, 152, 155, 160, 171, 236), NOT COUNTED falls from 31 to 16, and the replay reproduces 386 of 387 stored statuses (the one differing tag is the same before and after); in 42373 no tag changes on either side and 304 of 304 stored statuses are reproduced. W1's note N1 on the plan: "compare" marks any following word as a root on either side, so a wrong word after "compare" no longer voids a tag that holds its core word; lenient, side-neutral, accepted. IN PART, because no run has been made since the write. NOT CHECKED by W3: audit 42332; the Library Check hashes. Open: two clean live runs.$t$,
  '12124, 12125, 12133, 12150, 12151, 12152, 12158, 12159',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$W4's write card (cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58Y7MfUUirv95My9EkYLn2SW, "Write ASK 653 to the live engine?"): he pressed "Write it" at 09:27 CST 2026-11-25. The card and the message above it were read by W3 by message id; the press time is from Wall 12150; W3 did not read the press. There was no build card: the build was offline files only, and the card came after the build grade.$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "question": "Write ASK 653 to the live engine?", "options": {"Write it": "Shared Library changes two lines; a whole lexicon quote no longer voids the Oracle's word layer. W1 reads it back.", "Hold": "Next run keeps marking such layers NOT COUNTED (15 Oracle layers in 42528, told to judges as no footing)."}, "thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58Y7MfUUirv95My9EkYLn2SW", "press_time": "09:27 CST 2026-11-25", "message_above_the_card": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo581cGyZNzm1WTx62AT777PXT", "source": "the card and the message above it, read by W3 by message id; press time from Wall 12150; W3 did not read the press."}$j$::jsonb,
  'W4',
  $j${"md5": "fefa1ca530b8e59f6f7d9d7a0e61fc75", "path": "ask653/w4/plan653.md", "note": "plan rev 0, graded PASS WITH N1 by W1 (Wall 12125); N1 met in the build (Wall 12133).", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 12125, 12133"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"path": "ask653/w4/b1/b653.cjs", "md5": "b51d91b72b0d235f90a43e038ca82e5b", "what": "build script"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/line146_before.txt", "md5": "0f35069370a8748f4493d81d069afad4", "what": "anchor for the build script (LIB line 146 before)"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/tg/live_50ade174.json", "md5": "4bf159e462b3843fe283c7255ac8f6d7", "what": "base, live engine 50ade174"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/tg/target_engine_653.json", "md5": "bd0951795d911f08a2617a6c0b204000", "what": "target engine (written)"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/tg/target_engine_651_652_653.json", "md5": "f1e08aa62506e8f57097706c0f3e1355", "what": "earlier folded build on target 1aa15175 (not written; equal Shared Library by W4's build notes)"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/t653.cjs", "md5": "399ca8db12128e35f6802754652dc3a8", "what": "test"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/out_t653.txt", "md5": "d0728b0e936538c987f21f833b9b3265", "what": "test output"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/fx_42528.json", "md5": "d87d382969ffaa8b0832743d53a5da7e", "what": "fixture, L2 Count Plan output of run 42528"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/fx_42373.json", "md5": "6b37b15bd1859a84037fc5e6d913171f", "what": "fixture, L2 Count Plan output of run 42373"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/l2_42528_before_after.txt", "md5": "3e37eb6f13b1b84bbef0bae3562eba91", "what": "[L2] check before and after, every tag, run 42528"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/l2_42373_before_after.txt", "md5": "6d35f51750908cdf96559bce3115f38e", "what": "[L2] check before and after, every tag, run 42373"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/b1/build_notes.md", "md5": "ee493982db045c5a7eadbb029e434a25", "what": "build notes"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/write/fetchback_eng_653.json", "md5": "d8754ab149abeca8504c2e28a11ebfbc", "what": "fetch-back after the write"}, {"path": "ask653/w4/write/write653.sh", "md5": "3aeb0b19edcfe5eaa68e64fda81c50de", "what": "write script"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"engine": "ask653/w4/write/revert_eng_653.json, md5 5c9fe31950f71dec137dd770c8173e89 (restores 50ade174 by W4's post)", "child": "not written; nothing to revert", "database": "not written; nothing to revert", "rehearsed": "not stated in the posts W3 read", "source": "Wall 12150; md5sum by W3"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N1 (plan rev 0)", "wall_id": 12125, "md5_graded": "fefa1ca5", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 12125"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (build b1)", "wall_id": 12133, "md5_graded": "bd095179", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 12133"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (written target check with the full md5, made after the write: equal to live a5c3001d, 426 nodes, 0 parameter differences, connections equal)", "wall_id": 12159, "md5_graded": "bd0951795d911f08a2617a6c0b204000", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 12159, item 3"}]$j$::jsonb,
  ARRAY['bd0951795d911f08a2617a6c0b204000'], '[42332]'::jsonb,
  $j$[{"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "ORACLE_DEBATE_V1 moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN, node Shared Library (LIB lines 146 and 153)", "before": "version 50ade174; markRoots marks a word as a root only when it directly follows \"from\", \"root\", \"derived from\", \"cognate of/with/to\" or \"related to\"", "after": "version a5c3001d-c12d-4193-bf31-70bd63d8e3a5, 426 nodes; ROOTPRE also takes \"compare\" and \"akin to\" and allows \"variation of\", \"derivative of\", \"prolonged form of\" and \"form of\" after a marker; rootAt pass 2 takes a word joined by \"and\" or \"or\" to a root as a root (both tagged ASK 653); no LIB line added or removed; 46 MAP lengths re-measured; LIB f73f1bddf5d16f0e, map c9d27dc9f026361c"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"name": "t653.cjs on the build", "result": "14 PASS, 0 FAIL: the 42528 replay reproduces 386 of 387 stored statuses; the changed tags are exactly 88, 90, 91, 99, 101, 107, 108, 112, 113, 151, 152, 155, 160, 171 and 236, every change NOT COUNTED to COUNTED, all defender; two more tags change root marks and keep their status (110, 172); the 42373 replay reproduces 304 of 304 and changes no tag; \"compare\" marks a root and the number stays core; \"and\" between two numbers marks no root; \"and\" with no root before it marks no root; N1: a tag with only an absent \"compare ἄνθρωπος\" stays NOT COUNTED", "source": "ask653/w4/b1/out_t653.txt (read whole by W3); run by W1, Wall 12133"}, {"name": "t651_652.cjs on the target", "result": "ALL PASS (28)", "source": "W4's build notes; Wall 12133"}, {"name": "Standing set with child aad0ad9c", "result": "31 PASS, 0 FAIL on the target (W1, Wall 12133), before and after the write (W4, Wall 12150) and on live (W1, Wall 12152); pair Library Check PASSES; one-copy check PASS", "source": "Wall 12133, 12150, 12152"}, {"name": "NOT RUN", "result": "any live call", "source": "Wall 12150"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "result": "PASS (W1's fetch of live a5c3001d equals its own rebuild, W4's target bd095179 and W4's fetch-back d8754ab1: 426 nodes, 0 differences, connections equal; against 50ade174 only the Shared Library differs; standing 31 PASS 0 FAIL). The full target md5 is stated at Wall 12159 item 3.", "wall_id": 12152, "source": "Wall 12152 item 1 (commit 52e8530b); Wall 12159 item 3"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"case": "NO RUN YET.", "runs": [], "mark_for_the_next_run": "in the [L2] CHECK, a tag whose lexicon line is quoted whole (with \"from X and Y\", \"compare X\", \"akin to X\" or \"a variation of X\") is COUNTED when its Strong's number is in the cited verse.", "not_shown": "the changed root marking on a live run.", "source": "Wall 12150"}$j$::jsonb,
